  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water for Sustainable Growth 2015-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water for Sustainable Growth supports activities to provide Australian expertise on climate-resilient water management and WASH. The principal activity supported from 2018-19 is Phase 2 of the Australian Water Partnership (AWP), which links Australian expertise with partners in the Indo-Pacific to co-create policies, practices and tools, and build capacity and partnerships for climate-resilient water management. The investment also supports grants to: the International River Foundation 22nd International River Symposium; a meeting of the Sherpas for the High Level panel on Water supported by the International Water Centre; the Building healthy sustainable communities through good water stewardship services grant via Water Stewardship Australia Ltd; and support to expand the work of the India-Australia Water Science and Technology Partners</narrative>
  </description>
